WEBVTT

00:23.620 --> 00:25.290
All ships, fall back!

00:25.290 --> 00:29.000
Put distance between us so we don't get hit 
by the light, and continue our assault!

00:29.000 --> 00:31.510
MARIA, how are Shido, Tohka, and the others?

00:31.800 --> 00:33.650
<i>I still don't know.</i>

00:33.650 --> 00:36.420
<i>That object is disrupting my visuals.</i>

00:36.900 --> 00:41.390
<i>Furthermore, what appears to be a different 
Angel has manifested on the surface.</i>

00:41.390 --> 00:43.140
<i>Please analyze them quickly.</i>

00:43.450 --> 00:47.770
Rei-nyan is gone, so I guess 
I'm the only one who's free.

00:48.300 --> 00:50.340
I'll figure it out somehow with Spirit Power!

00:52.030 --> 00:52.690
Shido.

03:02.940 --> 03:04.100
Captain!

03:04.100 --> 03:05.200
We're almost there!

03:05.200 --> 03:08.620
We just need to make it 
to that ship called Fraxinus!

03:12.110 --> 03:12.830
Huh?

03:13.530 --> 03:14.860
Is this?

03:15.290 --> 03:17.180
Captain Kusakabe, right?

03:17.180 --> 03:19.600
We heard from Tobiichi.

03:19.600 --> 03:21.130
A-And you are?

03:21.620 --> 03:24.720
Hinako Shizaki, crew member of Fraxinus.

03:24.720 --> 03:28.920
We used our teleporter 
to transfer you all into the ship.

03:28.920 --> 03:32.450
Now, bring your soldiers 
and Artemisia this way.

03:33.020 --> 03:34.460
Y-Yes.

03:34.460 --> 03:35.850
They're my precious friends.

03:35.850 --> 03:36.900
Please take care of them.

03:37.270 --> 03:40.150
I can't make you any promises, 
but we'll do everything we can.

03:51.630 --> 03:53.570
Welcome to Fraxinus.

03:54.410 --> 03:56.040
I'm the commander, Kotori Itsuka.

03:56.900 --> 04:00.780
I'm Ryoko Kusakabe, 
former member of the JSDF AST.

04:01.260 --> 04:01.800
Wait!

04:02.100 --> 04:04.050
Y-You're the commander?!

04:04.410 --> 04:07.810
Oh, there's a nostalgic reaction.

04:07.810 --> 04:12.460
We've all gotten used to it, 
but normally it would be impossible.

04:12.460 --> 04:15.360
Having a middle school girl 
as our commander and all.

04:15.360 --> 04:16.300
Ahem!

04:17.610 --> 04:18.690
Pardon me.

04:18.690 --> 04:19.880
Please forgive me

04:19.880 --> 04:24.200
for foolishly trying to judge your capability 
based on your age and appearance.

04:24.740 --> 04:27.090
I'm grateful for your flexibility.

04:27.680 --> 04:30.250
Though I'm sorry we don't have the leeway

04:30.250 --> 04:33.310
to hold a welcoming party 
now that you've joined us.

04:33.310 --> 04:34.810
Don't worry about it.

04:34.810 --> 04:36.810
I understand the circumstances.

04:37.330 --> 04:38.480
Thank you.

04:38.480 --> 04:40.980
We've finished retrieving Artemisia.

04:40.980 --> 04:41.840
Kannazuki,

04:41.840 --> 04:43.800
you're all set, aren't you?

04:43.800 --> 04:45.060
We're cutting through.

04:45.060 --> 04:45.860
Yes.

04:45.860 --> 04:47.590
Leave it to me, Commander.

04:48.350 --> 04:50.460
Huh?!

04:53.230 --> 04:55.370
C-Captain Kannazuki!

04:55.370 --> 04:57.650
What are you doing here?!

04:57.650 --> 05:00.610
Ohh, long time no see, Kusakabe.

05:01.470 --> 05:02.860
Kannazuki...

05:03.430 --> 05:04.740
Captain?

05:06.110 --> 05:10.460
He was captain of the AST 
when I was first stationed with them!

05:10.870 --> 05:14.340
He was the squad's indisputable top ace.

05:14.340 --> 05:16.740
Wow, that man was?

05:16.740 --> 05:18.250
That's kind of cool, isn't it?

05:18.570 --> 05:22.000
You used to do that, Kannazuki?

05:22.280 --> 05:26.760
I always thought you were just someone 
the Commander picked up off the street.

05:26.760 --> 05:29.510
Commander Itsuka, this man is dangerous!

05:29.870 --> 05:31.420
He's the kind of pervert who dreams

05:31.420 --> 05:34.010
about having a middle 
school girl kick him in the butt!

05:34.010 --> 05:37.460
He would launch "protect middle school 
girls meetings" during our missions,

05:37.460 --> 05:40.050
and when he watched local 
middle schoolers going to school

05:40.050 --> 05:43.030
he got reported as a suspicious individual!

05:43.030 --> 05:45.530
You're right in his strike zone, Commander!

05:45.530 --> 05:46.960
How rude!

05:46.960 --> 05:49.530
Lately I prefer them stepping on me 
with the heel of their feet!

05:49.530 --> 05:51.740
It's somewhat plain, but quite superb...

05:55.370 --> 05:57.250
We have no time!

05:57.250 --> 06:00.370
MARIA, punch through 
the DEM ships ahead of us.

06:00.370 --> 06:02.300
We're launching an attack on Mio.

06:02.300 --> 06:05.260
<i>Roger, authorizing activation of Gungnir.</i>

06:05.260 --> 06:07.520
What are you doing still sleeping?

06:07.520 --> 06:11.850
Ratatoskr doesn't pay you to take naps.

06:11.850 --> 06:13.260
Thank you very much.

06:13.570 --> 06:15.520
Now, let's go, MARIA.

06:15.970 --> 06:17.560
For the sake of the Spirits,

06:17.560 --> 06:22.090
and above all, for more rewards 
from our Commander!

06:23.470 --> 06:24.960
Captain...

06:24.960 --> 06:28.510
Are you serious about that guy 
being our top ace?

06:28.990 --> 06:30.360
I'm serious.

06:30.360 --> 06:34.560
But that Kyohei Kannazuki was known as 
"The Walking HR Complaint"

06:34.560 --> 06:40.020
and "The Man With Valued Skills, 
And Criminal Fetishes",

06:40.020 --> 06:43.630
so that Commander is something else 
for taming him to this degree.

06:44.040 --> 06:47.620
<i>Launching Yggdrafolium 1 through 15.</i>

06:47.620 --> 06:50.010
<i>I'll drive away the enemy ships before us.</i>

06:50.010 --> 06:52.550
<i>Once we pass through, support the Spirits.</i>

07:09.740 --> 07:11.360
Analysis complete!

07:11.640 --> 07:13.650
Though what is all this?!

07:13.650 --> 07:14.870
What's the matter, Nia?

07:14.870 --> 07:18.000
What's the matter is whatever is 
going on with that Angel!

07:18.000 --> 07:20.000
It couldn't be anymore dangerous!

07:20.290 --> 07:23.180
That light causes all living creatures 
without exception to die,

07:23.180 --> 07:25.000
and all objects to break.

07:25.000 --> 07:28.530
It's like it's reducing everything's lifespan

07:28.530 --> 07:31.930
or durability to zero in an instant.

07:31.930 --> 07:35.300
To put it simply, it's an instant death beam?

07:35.300 --> 07:38.740
This would definitely get rejected 
if it were drawn in a manga.

07:38.740 --> 07:41.310
How are we supposed to defeat that?!

07:41.310 --> 07:43.620
As for the other thing...

07:43.620 --> 07:47.690
It's like that region around her 
is a completely different world.

07:48.050 --> 07:52.210
If we got a little closer I might be able 
to make out what it's like inside, but...

07:53.240 --> 07:56.740
<i>Kotori, I propose that we 
disconnect the sections</i>

07:56.740 --> 07:59.660
<i>containing that unconscious woman we just 
received and the non-combatants,</i>

07:59.660 --> 08:02.460
<i>ejecting them to Ulmus.</i>

08:02.770 --> 08:04.110
MARIA...

08:04.110 --> 08:06.570
<i>Of course, I have no intention of losing.</i>

08:06.990 --> 08:09.020
<i>It's merely for risk reduction.</i>

08:10.370 --> 08:12.020
Thank you, MARIA.

08:12.020 --> 08:14.300
For taking initiative to propose it.

08:14.300 --> 08:18.620
<i>No, it's only natural since an AI's 
processing speed is faster than humans.</i>

08:21.020 --> 08:23.850
Captain Kusakabe, you've heard the situation.

08:24.120 --> 08:27.540
Could I ask you to guard the ejected sections?

08:27.540 --> 08:28.500
That's...

08:29.250 --> 08:31.210
No, I understand.

08:31.630 --> 08:32.860
Good luck.

08:33.120 --> 08:36.210
Captain, you're a wonderful person.

08:36.210 --> 08:38.370
I definitely want you to work under me.

08:43.810 --> 08:47.250
Now, sorry everyone, but you're 
joining me on the path to hell.

08:47.680 --> 08:51.880
If you want to flee, you should 
follow those girls right away.

08:52.200 --> 08:54.510
What are you saying, Commander?

08:54.770 --> 08:57.890
After coming this far, 
we're with you all the way.

08:58.140 --> 09:02.140
For one thing, it's too dangerous to leave 
you alone with the Vice Commander.

09:02.420 --> 09:03.890
I know!

09:05.660 --> 09:07.090
All right.

09:07.090 --> 09:08.160
Then let's go.

09:08.160 --> 09:09.700
I love you all.

09:09.700 --> 09:10.440
Yes!

09:15.860 --> 09:19.090
<i>I've forced our way through 
the enemy ships' Territories.</i>

09:19.090 --> 09:21.200
<i>Kotori, ready the main cannon.</i>

09:27.010 --> 09:29.380
I've confirmed what's inside that space!

09:29.690 --> 09:33.580
At the center is Analyst Murasame—
No, Mio Takamiya!

09:33.580 --> 09:36.330
She's fighting Tohka and Tobiichi!

09:36.330 --> 09:37.630
What about the others?!

09:37.890 --> 09:43.210
Around her... Yoshino, Kaguya, Yuzuru, 
and Mukuro have fallen!

09:44.770 --> 09:46.890
There are no life signs!

09:46.890 --> 09:47.640
Huh?!

09:53.550 --> 09:55.650
Target: Mio Takamiya.

09:58.250 --> 10:00.740
Gungnir, fire!

10:04.480 --> 10:05.730
What's wrong?

10:05.730 --> 10:07.660
Aren't you coming after me?

10:07.660 --> 10:11.170
If you aren't, then I'll go ahead 
and come after you.

10:16.510 --> 10:17.570
Origami!

10:17.570 --> 10:18.380
I know!

10:19.590 --> 10:21.220
Sandalphon!

10:31.390 --> 10:33.070
Einherjar!

11:30.850 --> 11:31.820
Reine.

11:32.250 --> 11:35.470
No, I suppose I should call you Mio?

11:36.300 --> 11:38.550
Either one is fine.

11:41.250 --> 11:42.550
Reine.

11:42.550 --> 11:44.410
Was everything a lie?

11:44.410 --> 11:49.450
The fact that you saved me, 
the fact that you kept supporting me,

11:49.450 --> 11:52.190
and the fact that you 
called me your best friend.

11:52.560 --> 11:55.120
Were all of those, all of those a lie?

11:55.120 --> 11:56.610
It wasn't a lie.

11:57.110 --> 12:03.070
I treasure all of the Spirits, 
and I loved everyone aboard Fraxinus.

12:03.380 --> 12:07.630
And I still consider you 
my one and only best friend.

12:08.540 --> 12:09.460
It's just...

12:09.830 --> 12:14.650
I would consume even my best friend 
if I must to bring back Shin.

12:14.650 --> 12:15.960
That's all.

12:30.530 --> 12:32.970
How could you?

12:33.650 --> 12:36.570
That's absurd...

12:45.820 --> 12:46.940
Raphael!

12:47.950 --> 12:48.970
Nibeelcole!

12:53.360 --> 12:55.710
Leave it to me, Father!

12:57.540 --> 12:58.850
It's no use!

13:04.780 --> 13:06.280
Well?

13:06.280 --> 13:09.350
It's simple, but it's a not bad move, right?

13:11.060 --> 13:14.250
You've sure had your way with us until now.

13:14.250 --> 13:16.600
So it's time to take responsibility!

13:19.730 --> 13:20.850
Metatron!

13:28.560 --> 13:29.890
Huh? What?

13:29.890 --> 13:32.140
Did he wipe himself out with his own attack?

13:32.140 --> 13:35.210
Maybe he knew he didn't stand a chance 
against us and blew himself up?

13:35.900 --> 13:38.580
Hey, hey, Father, what do we do?

13:38.580 --> 13:40.840
Hmm, well...

13:44.620 --> 13:45.470
Huh?!

13:47.470 --> 13:48.520
What?!

13:48.520 --> 13:51.960
What am I doing attacking Father?!

13:51.960 --> 13:54.100
Rebelling? Is it my rebellious phase?

13:57.600 --> 13:58.980
Y-You!

13:58.980 --> 14:01.730
How dare you attack Father looking like me?!

14:02.080 --> 14:05.980
You used Haniel's power 
to transform into Nibeelcole?

14:05.980 --> 14:08.330
That's a smart play,

14:08.330 --> 14:11.120
but that also made it easy to predict.

14:12.770 --> 14:18.560
My Demon King, Beelzebub, allows me 
to know everything in this world.

14:18.560 --> 14:24.250
So naturally I looked into what kind 
of powers each Spirit possessed.

14:29.330 --> 14:31.970
It's about time to draw the curtain on this.

14:32.450 --> 14:38.770
I need to obtain the remaining 
Spirit Power before I encounter Deus,

14:39.550 --> 14:42.570
so I can create a new world.

14:43.460 --> 14:46.150
A new world?

14:46.590 --> 14:47.680
Yes.

14:47.680 --> 14:53.960
Me, Elliot, Ellen, and Karen are different 
from those manufactured Wizards.

14:53.960 --> 14:58.660
We're the true descendants 
of magic users, known as Magi.

14:59.150 --> 15:02.900
Though one day the humans who feared our power

15:02.900 --> 15:07.150
burned down our village and 
slaughtered everyone we knew.

15:08.340 --> 15:13.550
That's why we're going to overwrite 
this world using Deus' power,

15:14.050 --> 15:16.890
and get our revenge on humanity.

15:18.970 --> 15:23.060
Does that reasoning make it easier to accept?

15:23.450 --> 15:24.470
What?

15:25.070 --> 15:29.320
To be honest, my reason isn't all that grand.

15:29.890 --> 15:31.570
In my case,

15:31.570 --> 15:36.260
my standards for what I find enjoyable and 
unpleasant are slightly different from others.

15:36.260 --> 15:37.910
That's all it is.

15:38.500 --> 15:41.980
In all other regards, 
I'm not different from others.

15:41.980 --> 15:47.930
I'm just putting in honest effort in pursuit 
of my curiosity and the goals I seek.

15:48.330 --> 15:54.010
In that sense, I'm a perfectly average person.

15:54.340 --> 15:58.370
Now, we've talked for long enough.

15:58.370 --> 16:01.100
Farewell, Shido Itsuka,

16:01.460 --> 16:02.580
and

16:05.490 --> 16:07.110
Shinji Takamiya.

16:11.620 --> 16:12.840
Wh-What?!

16:13.890 --> 16:15.100
Natsumi?!

16:21.820 --> 16:23.670
Are you all right, Darling?!

16:23.670 --> 16:25.290
That was close.

16:25.290 --> 16:26.540
You were nearly a goner.

16:26.940 --> 16:27.890
I'm sorry.

16:27.890 --> 16:29.130
You saved me.

16:29.130 --> 16:32.500
What on earth is going on 
in this battle right now?!

16:32.500 --> 16:35.180
We've lost contact with everyone else...

16:35.180 --> 16:38.690
Also, isn't that the enemy's leader?

16:38.690 --> 16:40.620
I'll share the details later.

16:40.620 --> 16:42.810
The Spirit of Origin has manifested.

16:43.170 --> 16:46.560
I need to defeat him as quickly as possible 
so I can rejoin everyone else!

16:46.560 --> 16:49.190
Wha?! The Spirit of Origin?!

16:49.500 --> 16:52.500
Then we really do need to hurry!

16:52.500 --> 16:56.450
I'm kicking it up for everyone 
and you, Darling!

17:04.340 --> 17:08.040
Oh? Diva and Witch, huh?

17:08.040 --> 17:09.530
I'm happy.

17:09.530 --> 17:12.510
I'll be able to obtain two Sephirah too.

17:14.190 --> 17:16.350
What should we do, Darling?

17:17.060 --> 17:22.010
Should we attack the leader while 
you take down Nibeelcole?

17:22.940 --> 17:24.020
No.

17:24.020 --> 17:27.390
In order to defeat him, 
we'll need an attack he can't predict,

17:27.910 --> 17:31.090
or an attack he can't evade 
even if he can predict it.

17:31.570 --> 17:34.900
Both of you enhance me 
with Gabriel's performance.

17:35.170 --> 17:36.560
That'll be enough.

17:36.560 --> 17:37.410
Darling?

17:37.900 --> 17:40.380
Sounds like you have a plan.

17:40.380 --> 17:42.660
All right, be careful.

17:49.870 --> 17:51.850
Nothing you do is going to help!

17:51.850 --> 17:55.550
We'll make all three of you 
kneel before Father!

17:55.840 --> 17:57.050
Sandalphon!

18:00.160 --> 18:01.970
Halvanhelv!

18:22.460 --> 18:23.790
Father!

18:30.180 --> 18:34.600
Omniscience, the power to know 
absolutely everything.

18:34.600 --> 18:38.970
It seems you're still naive 
about what that means.

18:50.340 --> 18:54.610
Yeah, I figured you would 
block it, knowing you.

18:56.410 --> 18:59.120
You're right that it's only natural

18:59.120 --> 19:02.370
to look up the Angels' power 
as soon as you obtained Beelzebub.

19:02.370 --> 19:04.740
And since I'm not the original owner,

19:04.740 --> 19:07.870
of course the power is weakened when I use it.

19:08.830 --> 19:10.130
But you know what,

19:10.620 --> 19:13.130
did you learn this from Beelzebub?

19:13.130 --> 19:14.960
Did you look it up?

19:14.960 --> 19:18.450
Did you, omniscient Westcott?!

19:19.010 --> 19:20.140
What?

19:20.140 --> 19:24.300
Roaring Flash Blast Wave!

19:44.050 --> 19:44.820
Darling!

19:44.820 --> 19:45.810
Shido!

19:51.380 --> 19:54.020
Looks like you've beaten me.

19:56.330 --> 19:59.410
I guess this is the end of the line.

19:59.940 --> 20:02.530
It came surprisingly soon.

20:10.810 --> 20:14.180
Jeez, you surprised me.

20:14.180 --> 20:17.310
Yeah. I thought you would kill him.

20:18.100 --> 20:19.010
Yeah.

20:19.490 --> 20:20.980
I wanted to kill him.

20:21.500 --> 20:25.900
To be honest, I thought he might die 
when I fired off that last attack.

20:25.900 --> 20:28.140
That last attack?

20:28.140 --> 20:30.040
That Roaring whatever?

20:30.040 --> 20:31.580
Uhh, ahem.

20:32.630 --> 20:35.100
I'm not really sure what to say about this...

20:35.660 --> 20:39.470
but I think it would be wrong to kill him.

20:39.470 --> 20:41.780
I don't want to be like they were.

20:42.500 --> 20:44.500
Even if I feel bad toward Shinji for that.

20:45.490 --> 20:46.590
Darling.

20:47.420 --> 20:50.220
Well, that's fine too, then.

20:50.780 --> 20:52.780
Are you sure about this?

20:52.780 --> 20:55.730
You'll never get a chance like this again.

20:56.040 --> 20:57.360
Shut up.

20:57.360 --> 20:59.230
The loser doesn't get a say.

21:01.190 --> 21:04.600
You sound just like Elliot.

21:04.600 --> 21:06.430
What a shame.

21:06.430 --> 21:11.100
I was curious what death would feel like too.

21:20.740 --> 21:21.500
Wha?!

21:22.830 --> 21:23.610
Huh?

21:26.550 --> 21:28.140
Miku! Natsumi!

21:30.530 --> 21:31.530
Shin.

21:34.710 --> 21:35.580
Mio!

21:37.570 --> 21:39.900
Wh-Where is everyone...?

21:40.540 --> 21:42.870
I've recovered all the Sephirah.

21:43.310 --> 21:45.580
Along with their lives.

21:48.550 --> 21:52.180
Now we can be together forever, Shin.

21:52.790 --> 21:55.050
<b>Episode 7</b>

21:52.790 --> 21:55.050
<b>The World Tree Sheds Leaves</b>

23:25.050 --> 23:40.070
Episode 8 "The One Who Pulled the Trigger"

23:26.380 --> 23:30.050
Shido is thrown into despair 
at the deaths of his friends,

23:30.050 --> 23:32.780
but who appears in that final moment?

23:32.780 --> 23:36.640
Next time is Episode 8: 
The One Who Pulled the Trigger.

23:36.640 --> 23:39.370
Wipe away your tears, and fight, Shido.
